n administrative disposition skips completion verification … But the skip does not extend to the plan-review close gate (require_plan_review_for_close)'.","After this change the skip DOES extend to the plan-review gate for superseded/duplicate — the quoted help text becomes stale.","No acceptance criterion covers updating `rebar transition --help` or AGENTS.md."],"finding":"The change extends the administrative-disposition skip to the plan-review close gate for link-backed dispositions, which invalidates existing documentation: `rebar transition --help` currently states the skip covers 'completion verification' but NOT the plan-review gate, and AGENTS.md describes --force as the reserved path. No AC updates that help text / AGENTS.md.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f732c71491b0dfb9e","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why the existing escape does not cover it' and Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nee981a162edfd4d8","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator reads --help/AGENTS.md after the change and is told the skip does not cover the plan-review gate, contradicting the new behavior."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add: '- [ ] `rebar transition --help` and AGENTS.md are updated to state that live-link dispositions (superseded/duplicate) also skip the plan-review close gate, distinct from --force.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete audit-trail marker that distinguishes an evidence-backed link disposition close from a --force close (e.g. a recorded --class + a live-link reference on the close event) and add a proving command (`jq -e` on the close/transition record) that asserts it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1","E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The resulting close is distinguishable in the audit trail from a --force close (it is an evidence-backed disposition, not an unaudited bypass).'","No section of the body names the concrete artifact/field that makes the two closes distinguishable.","'distinguishable' is a subjective term with no named observable target or proving command."],"finding":"AC3 requires the evidence-backed close to be 'distinguishable in the audit trail from a --force close' but neither the AC nor the plan body specifies WHAT marker records this (a disposition class value, an evidence annotation, a log/event field), nor how a test would assert it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc7691b50f1ef9f5a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC3","norm_id":"nf32d08ef9c8ef773","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor implements the skip but cannot tell what value/field to write to satisfy the audit distinguishability requirement.","A reviewer cannot confirm AC3 is met because no concrete artifact is named to assert on."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Specify that the close records the disposition class and the satisfying supersedes/duplicates link id on the transition event, and add an assertion (e.g. jq on the event log) verifying that field is present for the evidence-backed close and absent/different for a --force close.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the concrete durable audit artifact that distinguishes an evidence-backed (skipped-plan-review) disposition close from a --force close — e.g. reuse the existing `completion-verifier: DISPOSITION <class>` disposition attestation, or emit a distinct plan-review-gate record — rather than relying on gate-skip alone.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC3: 'The resulting close is distinguishable in the audit trail from a --force close (it is an evidence-backed disposition, not an unaudited bypass).'","gates.close_plan_review_gate_check (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:92) verifies an already-created plan-review signature only; skipping it yields no plan-review attestation.","The DISPOSITION signal in close_disposition.decorate_manifest is on the completion-verifier attestation, not the plan-review one, so it does not automatically satisfy AC3 for the plan-review gate.","--force close audit is the FORCE_CLOSE comment at transition_close.py:519 with signatures withheld."],"finding":"AC3 requires the evidence-backed close be distinguishable in the audit trail from a --force close, but the plan does not specify the MECHANISM that produces that distinction for the plan-review gate specifically. Skipping the plan-review close gate leaves the ticket with NO plan-review attestation — the same absence a --force close leaves — so 'skip the gate' alone does not by itself create a distinguishable positive signal. The completion gate's existing `completion-verifier: DISPOSITION <class>` attestation (close_disposition.decorate_manifest) is a completion-verifier record, not a plan-review one, and a --force close writes a FORCE_CLOSE comment while withholding signatures. The plan should name the concrete durable artifact (e.g. reuse/emit a disposition-attestation record, or a distinct sidecar/manifest line) that marks the skipped-plan-review close as evidence-backed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f919de0ffeda85c6e","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC3 ('distinguishable in the audit trail from a --force close')","norm_id":"n9ff68d8b8d05f08a","priority":0.1222,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An auditor tries to tell an evidence-backed superseded close apart from a --force superseded close and finds both lack a plan-review attestation, with no other differentiating record specified by the plan."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_ac